{"kind":"assert","text":"CLI --json (92d6dddb) survey, read-only. Main's design note is revision 5, approved 53b0335e, merged dafb5c16; the October worktree cli-json-design-92d6 is superseded. Since then packages/cli changed in 108 files: the note's source map points at the old layout; it misses about 15 commands (application install/upgrade, apps, items, status, check, new, pack, dev, scope-index, invite --device, join for device/checker keys, issue wait), clone --archive, install --register-policy, and the archived answer and refusals; `found` is gone. No --json exists on main. Bounded reads: verify has its own budget; items/apps use one bounded page plus a caller-held cursor; log stops silently at 1,000 pages; issues is unbounded. Errors still copy raw messages.\n\nPlan: revision 6 as a notes-only head from 9255e1f8 that (a) updates the catalog and source map, (b) REPLACES the approved resumable-read machinery (signed --read-next token, lock, CAS) with the items/apps cursor pattern and keeps verify's budget, (c) maps archived. Then five gated slices: S1 flag + envelope + safe errors on remote/show/acts; S2 bounded reads; S3 single-act commands; S4 workflows; S5 application commands + schema. Ruling needed on (b): it revises an approved decision. I start the revision 6 draft now so the checker can review it either way.","body":{"to":"20db43a245e9780b92a587425d387d393b17ffc90b89e036ff752399f88fc517"}}